I am concerned that I have deceived myself.

When I look at my life in the harshest light, I am led to believe that I am a cruel and selfish person. I never make bad decisions - i always try and do right by everyone. I am always mediating, always connecting, always listening. But maybe I'm fed up with the way that people are hurt in spite of my intentions. Maybe I wish they made better choices. I can't control that, but... I worry that my decisions affect them still.

This leads me to believe I am a cruel and selfish person. Selfish people never get what they want, and I want to make the world better, relentlessly, at every turn. This is a cruel thing to describe because the world is tumultuous in its trajectory onward and upward to bright brilliant glory. Therefore, it is selfish of me to speak my intentions as if they were possible, plausible, or within my control - they are always possible, but it is selfish to describe them as such because they demand much. It is plausible, because it could happen with enough luck. And sometimes, not always but sometimes, it is within my control, and if it ever is, then sometimes I will succeed and sometimes I will fail. This means, sometimes I took something that was technically possible, described it as plausible, and then failed to make it happen.

This is why I try to think of myself as a teacher. If I don't have anything to teach, I don't go on cleric walks. I often talk to myself and whoever wants to hear. But it is abandoning my responsibilities when I don't build the systems, tools, or groups that could make the impossible possible, the implausible plausible, and the things that I wanted, real. It's my responsibility to make that chain happen, and I often just... Don't. I rely on others to do the hard parts. This is cruel and selfish. I wish it were not so, I do not delight in these two poor strategies that my fate has decided for me. Perhaps if my outcomes were better, I'd be more hateful or something. I don't think it needs to be that way but it often feels like that's how it is - fuel yourself with spite to make the world better, become comfy and content to drag everything down just a bit.

What is it all for?